{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath/schema/toolpath.schema.json","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:09:12.051809Z","id":"48ce3e9ae8e3946486738b61f1938455fbc4df9a9cc751d629f96a22564818c8","body":{"detail":"RFC.md (Path Parent table) says `uri` takes the `$ref` forms with no fragment, and that all three fields are required. Required is enforced only as key presence. Checked against this crate: `{\"uri\":\"\",\"path\":\"\",\"step\":\"\"}` and `{\"uri\":\"https://x/doc#frag\",\"path\":\"p\",\"step\":\"s\"}` both deserialize into `Parent`. `$defs/parent` has no `minLength` and no `pattern`, so `path p validate` accepts both in a .path.json file too. `Parent::new` (crates/toolpath/src/types.rs:480-489) also accepts empty strings. A reader resolving lineage then gets a document it cannot fetch, or an empty step id to classify against the parent's head, and the error shows up far from the writer that caused it. The RFC's no-fragment rule is stated in three places (RFC.md, the `Parent::uri` doc comment and the schema description) but enforced in none.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":338},"end":{"line":362},"content_hash":"f95c0573704e351b8fbae617e759d1f19fdf07b1fe2ab748737aaadb7eebd1f2"},"suggested_fix":"In `$defs/parent`, add `\"minLength\": 1` to `uri`, `path` and `step`, and `\"pattern\": \"^[^#]+$\"` to `uri`. Add a negative case for each to the schema tests in crates/path-cli/src/schema.rs. Optionally, reject empty fields when deserializing `Parent` in Rust, so .path.jsonl input (which skips the schema) is checked as well.","summary":"Nothing enforces the RFC's rules for parent: empty uri/path/step and a uri with a #fragment pass both serde and the schema","tags":["review","review:pr-354-qual-2","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath/schema/toolpath.schema.json","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:14:02.179363Z","id":"52aa890dda2357bc92c5a517a27b81bcf7f4f84712bf1341e9ac3280ac215d56","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath/schema/toolpath.schema.json:338-362: uri/path/step are plain {\"type\":\"string\"} with no minLength or pattern (the whole schema has no minLength and a single pattern, at line 16, for actor). RFC.md:724 says uri takes the $ref forms with no fragment. Scratch binary against this crate: {\"uri\":\"\",\"path\":\"\",\"step\":\"\"} => Ok and {\"uri\":\"https://x/doc#frag\",\"path\":\"p\",\"step\":\"s\"} => Ok. Parent::new at crates/toolpath/src/types.rs:482-488 copies the strings unchecked. concern is right: no user hits a failure before merge, but nothing enforces the stated rule.","kind":"comment","references":"48ce3e9ae8e3946486738b61f1938455fbc4df9a9cc751d629f96a22564818c8","summary":"confirmed: empty uri/path/step and a #fragment uri pass both serde and the schema","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
